{
  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2023-46361",
    "CVE-2026-38076"
  ],
  "description": "Zeng Yunxiang and Song Jiaxuan discovered that jbig2dec had an\nout-of-bounds read vulnerability in its command-line tool. An attacker\ncould possibly use this issue to cause jbig2dec to crash, resulting in a\ndenial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2023-46361)\n\nIt was discovered that jbig2dec had an integer overflow in the\njbig2_arith_iaid_ctx_new() function. An attacker could possibly use this\nissue to cause a denial of service. (CVE-2026-38076)",
  "id": "USN-8582-1",
  "isummary": "Several security issues were fixed in jbig2dec.",
